      ":question/problem": "The amount of charge stored in a battery is decreasing due to self-discharge. The rate at which the amount of stored charge decays $W(t),$ after $t$ months, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-0.025W.\n$$\n\nHow long does it take for the amount of stored charge to be $75%$ of the original amount? Round your answer to the nearest month."
